#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lexi - a fast, offline English dictionary for the terminal and a popup window.

Definitions come from Wiktionary (via kaikki.org) and Open English WordNet.
Any language Wiktionary has can be added for translations both ways.

  lexi WORD          print the definition in the terminal
  lexi               ask for a word and show it in a popup window
  lexi --open WORD   show WORD in the popup window
  lexi settings      open the settings (languages, font size, width) in the popup
  lexi --json WORD   print the lookup as JSON (for integrations such as Raycast)
  lexi --complete P  print words starting with P as JSON
  lexi update        download the dictionaries and (re)build the database
  lexi add LANG...   download dictionaries for languages, e.g. lexi add Danish Swedish
  lexi remove LANG   remove a language's dictionary
  lexi languages     list the installed languages (--all: every available language)
  lexi --help        show this help

In the popup: type a word and press Enter to look it up, or click a word.
← and → go back and forward, ↑ ↓ and the mouse wheel scroll, Ctrl+S opens
the settings and Esc closes.
"""
